/**
@page backends Backends: XDP and TC

BONet provides one backend header per hook type. Include the header for your
hook; it pulls in the rest of the library. A single source file includes only
one backend header.

@section backends_choice Backend headers

| Hook       | Header              | Context type           |
| ---------- | ------------------- | ---------------------- |
| XDP        | @c bnt_xdp.h        | @c struct @c xdp_md    |
| TC ingress | @c bnt_tc_ingress.h | @c struct @c __sk_buff |
| TC egress  | @c bnt_tc_egress.h  | @c struct @c __sk_buff |

@section backends_ctx Entry point

A program starts by parsing its outermost header. @c bnt_eth__parse() takes the
context and a starting offset and initializes a view:

@code{.c}
#include "bnt_xdp.h"

SEC("xdp")
int prog(struct xdp_md *ctx)
{
    bnt_eth eth;
    if (bnt_eth__parse(ctx, 0, &eth))
        return XDP_PASS;
    /* ... */
}
@endcode

On TC only the context type changes:

@code{.c}
#include "bnt_tc_ingress.h"

SEC("tc")
int prog(struct __sk_buff *skb)
{
    bnt_eth eth;
    if (bnt_eth__parse(skb, 0, &eth))
        return TC_ACT_OK;
    /* ... */
}
@endcode

Subsequent calls take views, not the context.

@section backends_same Backend portability

The API is identical across backends. Porting a program changes only the
included header and the context type. The only exception concerns explicit
checksum handling; see @ref modifying.
*/
